# The upstream source files are fetched, not tracked. They are large, they never
# change once downloaded, and a git repository keeps every version of everything
# forever, so each one added to the tree would sit in every future clone.
#
#   make data          fetch them and rebuild
#   make check         confirm they are the ones this repository was built from
#
# data/raw_manifest.json records the sha256 of each, and fetch_raw.py refuses to use
# a file that does not match. data/raw/README.md is the contract for adding new ones
# and stays in the repository.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/README.md

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# the test runner's dependencies
tests/node_modules/
